          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.1 Doubling a Square"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.364,
            0.846,
            0.404
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Baudhāyana’s Śulba-Sūtra (c. 800 BCE), Baudhāyana considers the following question:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.413,
            0.698,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? How can one construct a square having double the area of a given square?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.455,
            0.702,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A first guess might be to simply double the length of each side of the square. Will this new square have double the area of the original square?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.711,
            0.405,
            0.846,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.711,
                0.405,
                0.846,
                0.506
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_0_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.511,
            0.846,
            0.55
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It’s not hard to see that the new square will have area "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\times 2 = 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " times the area of the original square:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.245,
            0.569,
            0.401,
            0.719
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.245,
                0.569,
                0.401,
                0.719
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_0_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.493,
            0.558,
            0.753,
            0.755
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 12,
              "bbox": [
                0.493,
                0.558,
                0.753,
                0.755
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_0_image_12.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.767,
            0.845,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So how can one make a square that has double the area? Baudhāyana in his Śulba-Sūtra (Verse 1.9) gave an elegant answer to this question:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.825,
            0.828,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The diagonal of a square produces a square of double the area of the original square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.883,
            0.845,
            0.921
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As Baudhāyana says, the key is to construct a square on the diagonal of the original square:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
